  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Change to base $a$ and simplify. Assume $a>0$ and $a\\ne1$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\log_{a^2}a^3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac32$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{a^2}a^3&=\\frac{\\log_a a^3}{\\log_a a^2}\\\\\\log_{a^2}a^3&=\\frac{3\\log_a a}{2\\log_a a}\\\\\\log_{a^2}a^3&=\\frac32\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\log_{a^2}a^7$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac72$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{a^2}a^7&=\\frac{\\log_a a^7}{\\log_a a^2}\\\\\\log_{a^2}a^7&=\\frac{7\\log_a a}{2\\log_a a}\\\\\\log_{a^2}a^7&=\\frac72\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\log_{a^3}a^5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac53$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{a^3}a^5&=\\frac{\\log_a a^5}{\\log_a a^3}\\\\\\log_{a^3}a^5&=\\frac{5\\log_a a}{3\\log_a a}\\\\\\log_{a^3}a^5&=\\frac53\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{a}}\\sqrt[11]{a}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac3{11}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{a}}\\sqrt[11]{a}&=\\frac{\\log_a a^{1/11}}{\\log_a a^{1/3}}\\\\\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{a}}\\sqrt[11]{a}&=\\frac{\\frac1{11}\\log_a a}{\\frac13\\log_a a}\\\\\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{a}}\\sqrt[11]{a}&=\\frac{1/11}{1/3}\\\\\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{a}}\\sqrt[11]{a}&=\\frac3{11}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\log_a a^8-\\log_a a^7+\\log_a a^{11}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$12$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\log_a a^8-\\log_a a^7+\\log_a a^{11}&=(8-7+11)\\log_a a\\\\\\log_a a^8-\\log_a a^7+\\log_a a^{11}&=12\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\log_{\\sqrt a}\\sqrt[3]{a}+\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{a}}\\sqrt[4]{a}+\\log_{\\sqrt[4]{a}}\\sqrt[5]{a}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{133}{60}$\n\nChange each logarithm to base $a$, then simplify the fractional indices.",
          "worked": "Changing each term to base $a$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{\\sqrt a}\\sqrt[3]{a}&=\\frac{\\log_a a^{1/3}}{\\log_a a^{1/2}}\\\\\\log_{\\sqrt a}\\sqrt[3]{a}&=\\frac{1/3}{1/2}=\\frac23,\\\\\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{a}}\\sqrt[4]{a}&=\\frac{\\log_a a^{1/4}}{\\log_a a^{1/3}}\\\\\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{a}}\\sqrt[4]{a}&=\\frac{1/4}{1/3}=\\frac34,\\\\\\log_{\\sqrt[4]{a}}\\sqrt[5]{a}&=\\frac{\\log_a a^{1/5}}{\\log_a a^{1/4}}\\\\\\log_{\\sqrt[4]{a}}\\sqrt[5]{a}&=\\frac{1/5}{1/4}=\\frac45.\\end{align*}$$\nThe sum is\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac23+\\frac34+\\frac45&=\\frac{40+45+48}{60}\\\\\\frac23+\\frac34+\\frac45&=\\frac{133}{60}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
